     "note": "v5 (owner 13.11: both legs, a woman's walk): light quick steps on a narrow track with the hips swaying: a stride of 0.89 m in 0.93 s (129 steps a minute) while she travels 1.6 m. The dress is close and floor-length, so the step is short (a longer one stretches the cloth into a tent between the feet); the rest of the ground she still glides over (owner 12.11), but far less than before: v4 slid 0.92 m/s under a stride of 1.27 s"
